    <div class="op-faq-item">
     <details>
      <summary>Which models are available in the Omega Pull Series?</summary>
      <p>The OA100-SM Pull Series includes five model designations: PL-L, PL-R, PL-AA, PL-AM and PL-MA. These cover left-hand, right-hand and dual-door configurations.</p>
     </details>
    </div>

    <div class="op-faq-item">
     <details>
      <summary>What is the difference between PL-L and PL-R?</summary>
      <p>PL-L is the left-hand pull operator configuration, while PL-R is the right-hand pull operator configuration. Refer to the respective technical drawings to confirm the correct model for your door arrangement.</p>
     </details>
    </div>

    <div class="op-faq-item">
     <details>
      <summary>Are dual-door pull operator configurations available?</summary>
      <p>Yes. The Pull Series includes PL-AA for active/active, PL-AM for active/manual and PL-MA for manual/active dual-door arrangements.</p>
     </details>
    </div>

    <div class="op-faq-item">
     <details>
      <summary>What type of arm does the pull operator use?</summary>
      <p>The Surface Mount Pull Series uses a pull-side slide-track arm arrangement. The relevant model drawing should be reviewed for the specific mounting and installation details.</p>
     </details>
    </div>

    <div class="op-faq-item">
     <details>
      <summary>What is the maximum door weight capacity?</summary>
